  "scenario": "A parent is deciding whether a very cheap last-generation PlayStation would be a sensible first console for a teenager or whether moving to the current generation would avoid a false economy. The frozen corpus contains an anomalously cheap PlayStation 4 Pro bundle listing whose title says discontinued while its body says in stock, a separate seller-titled PS4-compatible controller listing, a flattened hardware comparison, general generation and backward-compatibility concepts, a historical PlayStation Network and PlayStation Plus snapshot, and two individual community posts. It contains no matched current PlayStation 5 offer, no inspection of the offered PS4 Pro unit, and no current authoritative compatibility or service matrix for the teenager's exact games, account, accessories, and region. The research problem is therefore to preserve exact model and listing boundaries, distinguish hardware mechanisms from game outcomes and ecosystem policy, and design a reversible teen-use trial or defer decision without naming a universal generation winner.",
