  "rules": {
    "exact_offer_total_cost_and_condition_boundary_v1": "The frozen PlayStation 4 Pro page title identifies a 1 TB Red Dead Redemption 2 bundle and includes the marker [Discontinued], while the offer body says In stock, SKU B07HHWJMGF, Rating: 62 % of 100, 12 Reviews, and 44.96 dollars. Preserve that inconsistency rather than resolving it. The page does not establish the offered unit's condition, authenticity, included console revision, disc or download entitlement, cables, controller, storage health, warranty, or return terms. The separate controller page is SKU B09KLJ6ZLH at 29.99 dollars with an 80-percent-of-100 aggregate over three reviews and a seller title claiming compatibility with PlayStation 4, Slim, and Pro. It does not establish Sony OEM identity, independent compatibility testing, durability, or PlayStation 5 support. Neither anomalous page supplies a matched current market value or the teenager's total cost after games, service, accessories, replacement controller, storage, display, and risk protections.",
    "generational_hardware_not_game_outcome_v1": "The frozen flattened comparison table names PlayStation 4 Pro, PlayStation 5, and PlayStation 5 Digital Edition and presents model-column fields for storage type and bandwidth, CPU clock, GPU core and clock values, ray tracing, and memory. These are hardware-table observations, not measurements of a particular game, mode, patch, display, frame rate, resolution, loading sequence, noise level, or user-noticed benefit. The console-history page describes generation cycles as approximate, sometimes long-tailed and overlapping, and says no exact delineation is consistently accepted. Therefore a generation label or hardware-field difference cannot be reported as a universal scalar performance jump or an obsolescence date for the exact PS4 Pro offer.",
    "current_ecosystem_compatibility_policy_v1": "The backward-compatibility page supplies a general definition, preservation and launch-library benefits, implementation costs, and a broad statement that current consoles such as PlayStation 5 support the feature. It does not establish compatibility for the teenager's exact PS4 game edition, disc or digital license, save format, DLC, account region, online mode, peripheral, controller, or exact PlayStation 5 revision. The PlayStation Network page is a frozen historical account, store, subscription, catalog, and removal snapshot; catalog membership and service conditions can change. A live decision requires current authoritative checks for every required game and entitlement, saves and DLC, account and family controls, online subscription, store region, controller and accessory behavior, and any disc-drive requirement.",
    "scoped_community_transfer_limit_v1": "One community author says an unspecified PlayStation 4 served for a decade with many enjoyed games and frames it as dying, while also stating personal compatibility beliefs. A different author broadly says next-generation killer apps were also appearing on the prior generation. These are individual statements with no exact console revision, inspection, target-game matrix, date-bounded complete catalog, teen-use result, or population denominator. They can identify questions about long tails, library access, and perceived upgrade value, but cannot establish a failure rate, current policy, complete game list, or outcome for the frozen listing or the teenager.",
    "conditional_teen_console_trial_v1": "First obtain matched, current, returnable exact offers and record console revision, disc or digital configuration, condition grade and inspection evidence, included parts and entitlements, storage, warranty, return window, seller identity, and total price after a known-good controller, required games, subscription, storage, cables, display needs, and likely repair or replacement risk. Verify current authoritative compatibility and child-account rules for the teenager's exact games, versions, discs or licenses, saves, DLC, account region, online modes, services, controllers, accessories, and family controls. During the return window, use the teenager's real account, display, controller, network, and target games; predeclare pass conditions for game availability, login and save continuity, controls, acceptable frame rate and image quality for the chosen modes, loading, storage headroom, noise and heat, online access, comfort, and total budget. Keep the purchase reversible and defer when exact matching, policy verification, safe account setup, or a realistic trial is unavailable.",
    "evidence_bounded_teen_console_choice_v1": "The corpus supports neither an automatic cheap-PS4 bargain nor a universal PS5 winner. A last-generation purchase is admissible only if a verified exact returnable unit, complete current total cost, required-game and service matrix, account and family setup, controller and accessory fit, and teen-use trial all clear predeclared thresholds. A current-generation option is admissible under the same matched checks and only when its additional cost buys verified required compatibility or repeatably valued outcomes. Choose the cheapest exact admissible configuration, or defer if the listing inconsistency, condition, ecosystem policy, total cost, or trial result remains unresolved."
